Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:43:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 18/20] Worker process: the application runs from a copy of
 bin, as ASP.NET's shadow copies

On .NET Framework ASP.NET runs an application from shadow copies of bin's assemblies,
and its worker process (w3wp) stays while the application restarts. Applications write
into bin (DNN's installers copy module DLLs there): the assemblies a .NET process has
loaded are locked on Windows ("being used by another process") and would be overwritten
in place on Linux.

WebFormsProcess.RunInWorker: the process stays and runs the application in a child
process from a copy of bin; an application restart (exit code 75) starts it again from
a new copy. SIGTERM/SIGINT are passed on. WEBFORMSFORCORE_SHADOWCOPY=0 runs it in place.
In the worker, the application's root is given (WEBFORMSFORCORE_APP_PATH);
HttpRuntime.BinDirectory stays the application's bin (where it writes), the runtime
loads from the copy (BinDirectoryInternal).
